  "_meta": {
    "version": "2.0.0",
    "domain": "fdm",
    "description": "Printer capability roster for material feasibility and design-for-manufacturing decisions. Since 2026-10-12 each printer's row is its id and display name; the capability profile itself (ceilings, build volume, chamber, tolerance, speed, layer ladder, supported materials) is the printer's catalogue record, served one printer at a time by Kiln and read through kiln.design_intelligence.get_printer_design_profile. The generic 'default' row stays whole.",
    "_split_note": "The roster and the generic floor ship here.  A printer's profile is its catalogue record's (fetched when the printer is set up, kept on this computer); engineering depth (how each printer actually behaves and what to design for) is available in Kiln Pro; see https://kiln3d.com/pricing.",
    "_default_profile_note": "The 'default' entry is the deliberately conservative stand-in for a printer Kiln has no record for here: a printer it has no profile for, or a catalogued printer on an install that is signed out. Its numbers are the floor a commodity FDM machine can be assumed to meet -- the same hotend and bed ceilings the generic safety profile states -- NOT a measurement of any product, so a feasibility answer given against it is the answer for the least capable plausible machine. Register the real printer (and sign in) to get a real answer."
  },
